# THE #694 REVIEW BLOCK, AND THE ONLY FIXTURE HERE WHOSE TWO ASSERTIONS DISAGREE
# ABOUT WHICH REF IS MEANT. `git checkout -b w5-g3-tail origin/main` with
# `branch.autoSetupMerge` unset -- git's own default -- sets
# `branch.w5-g3-tail.merge = refs/heads/main`, so `@{u}` names `origin/main`
# and NOT this branch's own remote branch. A check reading `@{u}` counts main's
# own new commits as `behind` and REFUSES a branch with nothing wrong with it,
# saying "no push makes `## Head` the pull request's head" -- which is false
# there, because the pull request's head ref is `refs/heads/w5-g3-tail` and a
# push to it is exactly the repair.
#
# HOW TO FIND THIS CONFIGURATION, rather than a count that decays the moment a
# seat pushes with `-u`: `git config --get branch.<name>.merge` not equal to
# `refs/heads/<name>`. It was live in the fixer's clone when this was written,
# on a branch a seat was running in at that moment.
#
# `@{u}` is not among the fields below, and removing it from the input set is
# the whole repair: the compared ref is a function of the branch's name and its
# remote. So this branch is compared against `origin/w5-g3-tail`, which is 2
# commits behind HEAD -- the WARN arm -- while `@{u}` would have made it 1
# behind and 1 ahead, which is the refusing arm.
#
# <branch or -> <remote or -> <own-remote-ref sha or -> <behind> <ahead> <rc> <compared ref or -> <text>
w5-g3-tail origin 9f8e7d6c5b4a392817065f4e3d2c1b0a98765432 0 2 4 origin/w5-g3-tail a branch tracking main is compared against its own remote branch, not @{u}
